      "message": "The critical thing to point out here is that\n\npackages/modules/Connectivity/bpf_progs/bpf_shared.h:154\n\nalready has:\n\ntypedef struct {\n    // Allowed interface index. Only applicable if IIF_MATCH is set in the rule bitmask above.\n    uint32_t iif;\n    // A bitmask of enum values in UidOwnerMatchType.\n    uint32_t rule;\n} UidOwnerValue;\nSTRUCT_SIZE(UidOwnerValue, 2 * 4);  // 8\n\nwhich means all the static_cast\u003cuint8\u003e where in a sense outright wrong.\n\nIt looks like that\u0027s been the case since\n\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/netd/+/6a84ce13292c3fd07601eb1a818ae363eb386c2c%5E%21/\n\nbpf_shared.h - add asserts for size of structures\n\nThis is to make sure we maintain compatibility between C/C++ and Java.\n\nAs a side effect we change a uint8 to a uint32, and add 3 explicit padding bytes.\n\n---\n\nI made that change from u8 to u32 in order to avoid adding char pad[3] at the end of the struct, but I failed to follow through on the users...\n\nIt doesn\u0027t really matter, but we do have to fix it.",
